## 4. RED-PROOF SABOTAGE A — ticket single-use

Condition asserted: `TicketStore.verifyTicket` is consume-on-verify — the
first call returns the binding, the second call throws `reused-ticket`.

Sabotage (minimal, in `dispatcher/src/approval-tickets.ts::verifyTicket`):
removed the `record.used = true;` burn so reuse succeeds.
```diff
diff --git a/dispatcher/src/approval-tickets.ts b/dispatcher/src/approval-tickets.ts
@@ -115,7 +115,7 @@ export class TicketStore {
       this.tickets.delete(token);
       throw new TicketError("expired-ticket", "approval ticket has expired");
     }
-    record.used = true;
+    // SABOTAGE-A: consume-on-verify disabled (red-proof)
     return { taskId: record.taskId, subjectHash: record.subjectHash };
```

Failing run: `bun test dispatcher/test/server-api.test.ts` → EXIT 1
```
 171 |   test("verifyTicket consumes on first use and rejects reuse", () => {
 ...
 176 |     expect(() => store.verifyTicket(token)).toThrow(/already been used/);
                                                   ^
 error: expect(received).toThrow(expected)
 Expected pattern: /already been used/
 Received function did not throw
 (fail) approval tickets: single-use + TTL > verifyTicket consumes on first use and rejects reuse
  19 pass
  1 fail
  69 expect() calls
 Ran 20 tests across 1 file.
```
→ Check is NOT vacuous: breaking single-use turns the suite red.

Restore: `git checkout -- dispatcher/src/approval-tickets.ts` → `RESTORED`,
`git status --short` → clean (empty).
Post-restore: `bun test dispatcher/test/server-api.test.ts` → EXIT 0,
`20 pass, 0 fail`. → PASS when restored.

