## 6. RED-PROOF SABOTAGE C — SSE replay gap marker

Condition asserted: `EventBus.replaySince` (surfaced via
`GET /api/events?snapshot=1`) emits a `fleet.gap` sequence-gap marker when
replay starts before the oldest buffered event after ring-buffer overflow,
so consumers detect the hole instead of silently missing history.

Sabotage (minimal, in `dispatcher/src/event-bus.ts::replaySince`): forced
`gap` to `null`, suppressing the marker.
```diff
diff --git a/dispatcher/src/event-bus.ts b/dispatcher/src/event-bus.ts
@@ -130,11 +130,8 @@ export class EventBus {
   replaySince(fromSeq: number): EventReplay {
     const start = Number.isFinite(fromSeq) ? Math.floor(fromSeq) : 1;
     const events = this.buffer.filter((event) => event.seq >= start);
-    const oldest = this.oldestSeq();
-    const gap: SequenceGap | null =
-      this.dropped > 0 && start < oldest
-        ? { fromSeq: start, toSeq: oldest - 1, dropped: Math.min(this.dropped, oldest - start) }
-        : null;
+    // SABOTAGE-C: gap marker suppressed (red-proof)
+    const gap: SequenceGap | null = null;
     return { events, gap };
```

Failing run: `bun test dispatcher/test/server-api.test.ts` → EXIT 1
```
 360 |     expect(body).toContain("event: fleet.gap");
                        ^
 error: expect(received).toContain(expected)
 Expected to contain: "event: fleet.gap"
 Received: "id: 3\nevent: probe\ndata: {...seq 3...}id: 4\nevent: probe\ndata: {...seq 4...}id: 5\nevent: probe\ndata: {...seq 5...}"
 (fail) GET /api/events SSE > snapshot replays from Last-Event-ID with a gap marker after overflow
  19 pass
  1 fail
  66 expect() calls
 Ran 20 tests across 1 file.
```
→ Check is NOT vacuous: a silent-history-hole bus turns the suite red.

Restore: `git checkout -- dispatcher/src/event-bus.ts` → `RESTORED`,
`git status --short` → clean (empty).
Post-restore: `bun test dispatcher/test/server-api.test.ts` → EXIT 0,
`20 pass, 0 fail`. → PASS when restored.

